From: EBAZ4205 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: zynq-ebaz4205: enable FCLK0 (fclk-enable=<9>)

The board dts set fclk-enable=<8> (FCLK3 only, the GbE PHY ref clock).
With FCLK0 excluded, Linux clk_disable_unused() gates it, freezing any PL
AXI interconnect clocked by FCLK0 -> every PS->PL AXI access hangs the A9
hard (JTAG halt then times out; only a power-cycle recovers). Enable FCLK0
too (<9> = FCLK0|FCLK3) so PL peripherals are reachable from Linux /dev/mem.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-ebaz4205.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/xilinx/zynq-ebaz4205.dts
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 &clkc {
 	ps-clk-frequency = <33333333>;
-	fclk-enable = <8>;
+	fclk-enable = <9>;
 };
 
 &gem0 {
